  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Leqvio (inclisiran) Criteria Version 1; Original 10/5/2022; Approval 11/18/2022; Effective 2023-01-02.",
    "Source FDA indication: adults with HeFH or clinical ASCVD requiring additional LDL-C lowering, as an adjunct to diet and maximally tolerated statin therapy. Effect on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality has not been determined.",
    "HeFH baseline LDL-C is before any lipid-lowering pharmacologic therapy. Confirmation routes and strict family age/LDL and Dutch score thresholds are attestations. LDL goals are <100 mg/dL for HeFH and <70 mg/dL for ASCVD.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval 6 months; reauthorization 12 months with chart notes indicating at least 10% reduction in LDL-C.",
    "Dosing/quantity (notes only): 284 mg as a single subcutaneous injection initially, again at 3 months, then every 6 months. HCPCS J1306 max of 284. max_units is null; quantity enforcement requires manual review.",
    "Cautions (notes only): common adverse reactions (≥3%) include injection site reaction, arthralgia, urinary tract infection, diarrhea, bronchitis, pain in extremity, and dyspnea. Inject subcutaneously only into abdomen, upper arm, or thigh.",
    "Remains partial: diagnosis, confirmation, submitted labs, therapy history, intolerance/contraindications and administration are attestations; evidence verification, cautions, duration, reauthorization and dosing/quantity require manual review. PDL status unknown. Praluent/Repatha is linked as an alternative, not concurrent therapy."
  ],
  "max_units": null,
